        </div>
        <!-- ⚠️ The row lives INSIDE the page width. It used to sit on a negative-margin row bled to the
             viewport edges, which stretched three slides across the whole screen.
             ⚠️ NO links anywhere: the arrows only move the track. The wrap is continuous because
             CLONES slides are copied to BOTH ends and the track resets onto the matching real slide
             with no transition once a clone is reached — identical frames, so the reset is invisible.
             CLONES must be >= the slides on screen at any width (3 / 1), so three covers both. -->
        <div class="car-shell">
          <button class="car-btn car-btn--prev" type="button" aria-label="Previous scene"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 6l-6 6 6 6" /></svg></button>
